=====================================
FOLDER: US_inter_alpha
SYSTEM: Vives — vives.uv.es
CREATED: 10/07/2026
UPDATED: 10/07/2026
PURPOSE: Umbrella-sampling stage seeded from 'SMD_inter_alpha''s 100 structures per
         edge/replica, holding each edge's driven CV (and dD=0) fixed at 100 evenly
         spaced values to reconstruct the interconversion free-energy profile via WHAM.
=====================================

10/07/2026

o Read (read-only, supervisor account on MareNostrum 5) the equivalent, already-running
  pph4 SMD->US->WHAM pipeline at 'LFER_3_mg2/pph4/US/' to use as the reference layout:
  a top-level folder holding 'USW_100_TSx_TSy/repN/' replicas (100 numbered window
  folders, an 'inputs/' template folder, a 'generate_US_window.py' generator, a
  'COLVAR/' folder and a 'WHAM/' folder) plus one shared 'WHAM_files/'. Reproduced that
  structure here rather than copying it directly, since pph3 alpha's atom-index scheme
  and per-edge wall definitions differ from pph4's.

o Set up 'US_inter_alpha/' as a new top-level folder, parallel to 'SMD_inter_alpha/',
  with the same five edges. For each of the fifteen edge/replica combinations, built
  'inputs/plumed_USW_XX.dat' by taking that edge's own 'SMD_inter_alpha/<edge>/rep1/
  plumed_SMD_pph3-rep1.dat', stripping the MOVINGRESTRAINT block and the SMD-only PRINT
  lines, and replacing them with a single static restraint on that edge's driven CV
  ('uw: RESTRAINT ARG=<CV> AT=XX KAPPA=KAPPA_kcal') plus the pre-existing 'dD=0' pin —
  everything else (atom groups, CVs, edge-specific walls) carried over unchanged.

o Wrote 'inputs/US_lammps.in' (800,000-step run per window, same NNP committee and
  timestep as the SMD stage) and 'inputs/job_lammps-deepmd.sh' (adapted from the SMD
  stage's Vives job script — same 'cuerda' GPU partition and DeePMD-kit 2.1.4 conda
  environment, but computing its EXTRA_FILES list at run time so the one script works
  unchanged for every window). Copied each replica's 100 seed structures from
  '../SMD_inter_alpha/<edge>/repN/lmp_files/' into 'inputs/lmp_files/'.

o Wrote one 'generate_US_window.py' per edge/replica (adapted from pph4's version),
  with the window range set to that edge's own SMD pull range (AT0->AT1), kappa=300
  kcal/mol for every static restraint, and WHAM histogram parameters EQUIL_FRAMES=100,
  CV_BIN_WIDTH=0.01, NUMBER_OF_CV_BINS=250, MIN_CV_VALUE = (window minimum - 0.45) —
  the last chosen to give the WHAM histogram a comfortable margin below (and, given the
  250-bin/0.01 span, well above) each edge's sampled range, mirroring pph4's convention.

o Copied 'wham1D.py' and 'errors_wham1D.py' from the MareNostrum 5 pph4 project into a
  new shared 'WHAM_files/' here (no prior copy existed anywhere on Vives), and wrote a
  Vives-adapted 'job_wham.sh' mimicking the same ArcaNN job-script framework used by the
  SMD stage, on the 'cuerda' qos/partition, activating the 'wham_miguel' conda
  environment (already has a compatible numpy/scipy/matplotlib) instead of loading
  DeepMD-kit.

o Ran 'generate_US_window.py 100' in all fifteen 'USW_100_<edge>/repN/' folders,
  producing 1500 window folders total (100 per replica) plus each replica's
  'WHAM/input.txt' and 'WHAM/job_wham.sh'. Spot-checked restraint values, dD pinning,
  byte-identical seed structures and WHAM input headers/centers across several
  edges/windows — all correct.

o Initially only copied the per-window 'job_lammps-deepmd.sh' convenience script into
  each of the 1500 window folders (as pph4 itself does), missing the piece that
  actually drives a replica's 100 windows in practice: fetched and read pph4's
  'job-array_lammps-deepmd_explore_gpu_alogin1.sh' (living at the replica top level, one
  per replica) to see it's a SLURM job array (--array=0-99) that uses
  '' to cd into the matching window folder and run that window's
  own 'US_lammps.in'/'plumed_USW_NNN.dat'/'USW_NNN.lmp'. Wrote the Vives equivalent,
  'job-array_lammps-deepmd_explore_gpu_vives.sh', one per replica (fifteen total, at
  each 'USW_100_<edge>/repN/' top level) — same 'cuerda' qos/partition and DeePMD-kit
  2.1.4 conda activation as the SMD stage's job script, '--array=0-99%10' by default
  (edit the array range to resubmit a subset of windows), NNP graph paths already
  absolute inside 'US_lammps.in' so no per-task model symlinking is needed. This is the
  one to actually 'sbatch' per replica; the per-window 'job_lammps-deepmd.sh' copies
  remain as a fallback for resubmitting a single window by hand.

o No SLURM jobs were submitted; the LAMMPS US windows and the WHAM reconstruction are
  left for manual submission once reviewed.
